<div class="row">
  <div class="small-12 columns">
    <br />
    <h2>What is HB2?</h2>
    <div class="indent">
      <p>If you're looking to learn more about HB2, here's some useful links:</p>
      <ul class="list">
        <li>The <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Public_Facilities_Privacy_%26_Security_Act" class="link" target="_blank">Wikipedia page on HB2</a> includes a very detailed and well sourced account of the bill and it's history.</li>
        <li>Here's the <a href="<%= asset_url('pdf/H2v4.pdf') %>" class="link" target="_blank">full text</a> of the bill. You can see that this is version 4, there are 3 previous versions also available: <a href="<%= asset_url('pdf/H2v1.pdf') %>" class="link" target="_blank">v1</a>, <a href="<%= asset_url('pdf/H2v2.pdf') %>" class="link" target="_blank">v2</a>, and <a href="<%= asset_url('pdf/H2v3.pdf') %>" class="link" target="_blank">v3</a>.
        <small class="subtle"> Obtained via <a href="http://www.ncleg.net/" class="link" target="_blank">NCGA</a>.</small></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<hr />
<div class="row">
  <div class="small-12 columns">
    <br />
    <h2>Stop HB2</h2>
    <div class="indent">
      <p>Since HB2 came into existence, there are a lot of sites and protest movements that have sprung up around it. There many people working to stop this bill. Here's just a few of them:</p>
      <hr>

      <p>On Twitter, you can find the hashtags <a href="<%= hashtag_search_url('WeAreNotThis') %>" class="link" target="_blank">#WeAreNotThis</a>, <a href="<%= hashtag_search_url('RepealHB2') %>" class="link" target="_blank">#RepealHB2</a>, <a href="<%= hashtag_search_url('HateBill2') %>" class="link" target="_blank">#HateBill2</a>, <a href="<%= hashtag_search_url('YallMeansAll') %>" class="link" target="_blank">#YallMeansAll</a>, and many more cropping up each day.</p>

      <hr />
      <a href="http://startups-against-hb2.com/" class="link other-org" target="_blank">
